From 6c702f80d4596ec6c91cdf14f89adac384be748b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <contact@buildthings.co>
Date: Sat, 03 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash family for two DGX Sparks (TP=2, EXL3
 2.9 bpw)

families/deepseek_v41/: a CUDA engine for the MiaAI-Lab EXL3 2.9 bpw packs of
DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash over two DGX Sparks: CSA2 attention with FP8 KV rows and the
lightning indexer, Single-Pass mHC, Engram rows read from packed per-rank NVMe shards,
the routed experts on EXL3 kernels for GB10 (x3ld / x3seg / x3gm), exact DSpark
speculative decoding (drafted replies == serial replies), CED bounded-replay prefill,
a 4-slot batcher with a shared FP8 pool, sessions with an NVMe tier, prepared per-rank
folders for fast restarts, structured output, DSML tool calls, and an OpenAI API.

Also: the EXL3 linear's device-side skip (graph-safe), fp64 in the communicator's
dtype table, --kv-dtype fp8, extra model ids in /v1/models, the family's tests.

MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Jay Leaton (NOTICE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). No
draft-vocabulary ranking is shipped for TF_DSV41_DRAFT_HEAD=trim (off by default).
